      "next_deadline": "HHAP-6 application was due to HCD August 29, 2025; HHAP-7 allocations are preliminary for FY 2026-27. No local competitive process: HHSA programs the County share itself and the CoC programs the regional share.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "San Benito County is a small non-entitlement county with no housing department: the Resource Management Agency (Planning and Building, Abraham Prado, (831) 637-5313) administers the inclusionary ordinance, in-lieu fees, density bonus and TEFRA hearings; the Health and Human Services Agency (Community Services and Workforce Development) runs HHAP, the shelter and the Migrant Center; Behavioral Health holds BHSA; and the Housing Authority of the County of Santa Cruz administers vouchers and PBVs for Hollister and San Juan Bautista. The County has no HOME or CDBG entitlement, no housing trust fund NOFA and no County loan program; Hollister runs its own PLHA and CDBG programs (Pass 3). sanbenitocountyca.gov and the amlegal code library block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors packets on cosb.granicus.com (attachments on d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net), HCD allocation tables and hacosantacruz.org. HHAP is the County's only recurring homelessness money and it is fully committed to shelter operations, so it is not a capital or operating source for new PSH; a developer would need to negotiate with the Coalition of Homeless Services Providers for CoC-level funds or PBV referrals. Source is the August 26, 2025 Board packet; HHAP-6 and HHAP-7 figures from HCD allocation tables.",
